{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-commands/src/commands/connect.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T05:28:02.539532Z","id":"2e761f5d86bc3a6b99a0f90d101cf41d4d0b32bb63e19a09e9cc916ee82dcc7a","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-cli/src/commands/connect.rs:406-414, record 672e8ed0.\n\nThe continuation that issues tokens also rotates the continuation token, so a poll whose answer is lost on the wire leaves the client with a token the daemon no longer knows (401 invalid_token, or 409 already_issued). clax connect then forgets the request and its key and tells the person to have the owner revoke the connection in People; the next connect makes a new key and request. The stray grant signs nothing without the key. An answer that did arrive is never lost here: remote-pending.json is removed only after remote.json is saved (both written whole by write_private). Recovery today needs the owner.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:03275e894a555fae4b08ac4bddfee28327965aed","span":{"start":{"line":406},"end":{"line":414},"content_hash":"38a5aeac6bc7aaf40772b6316b28717047bfaf09232aa277f3bb3826a9b77aca"},"suggested_fix":"Idempotent re-issue: keep the hash of the pre-issue continuation token until the access token is first used (at most 10 minutes); a continuation call presenting it, signed by the grant's key with a later t, revokes the undelivered tokens and issues fresh ones in one transaction. Safe because the tokens are key-bound: a sniffer of the old token cannot sign, and accept_t refuses a replay.","summary":"A request whose tokens were issued to an answer that never arrived cannot be finished: its grant stays live until the owner revokes it or 30 days pass","tags":["spec:6.3","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-commands/src/commands/doctor.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T05:28:02.539595Z","id":"1063c57c400aed342a7fa85ad5b1baa80e3d4897960a6d09f628849c61e1d2eb","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-cli/src/commands/doctor.rs:730-730, record 30b40937.\n\nFailure: after an upgrade, before the daemon is replaced, `clax doctor` runs Store::open, which plans and records the backfill (seconds on a large home, with no progress shown). Changes the still-running older daemon makes after that plan are never recorded: they are not in the staging snapshot, and the older build records nothing live.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:03275e894a555fae4b08ac4bddfee28327965aed","span":{"start":{"line":730},"end":{"line":730},"content_hash":"e8cfaa20dc14468f4bef01aba5ada983db7554d9886c28787dbaec157f0587e0"},"suggested_fix":"Have doctor and init open the store without the backfill (or read-only) when the schema is behind and a daemon is running, and leave the backfill to the daemon's start, which reports progress.","summary":"clax doctor (and clax init's credential revoke) open the store directly, so the first run of a new build migrates to 23 and runs the whole backfill outside the daemon, silently, possibly under an older running daemon","tags":["review","migration","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-commands/src/commands/doctor_agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T05:28:02.539661Z","id":"00fbcba8d342c7dce3a2d2781f4f62c831d389eb339ca0193032ae85052fbde5","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-cli/src/commands/doctor_agent.rs:459-461, record 47eb01b7.\n\nNot taken (2026-10-01, docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-01-grok-build.md:114 (Q1)): doctor prints the approval line and never writes it. Writing it needs a comment-preserving TOML edit in clax init and a matching removal in clax uninit; the doctor's mcp detail and the READMEs then change.","kind":"alternative","ref":"git:03275e894a555fae4b08ac4bddfee28327965aed","span":{"start":{"line":459},"end":{"line":461},"content_hash":"ab384b31d810513ba2793692a27f8dac0f9118459eeaf07fe63eb2939829ea9f"},"summary":"Have clax init write Grok's tool approval, MCPTool(clax_grok__*), into ~/.grok/config.toml","tags":["revisit:the owner wants clax init to lift Grok's per-call approval","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-commands/src/commands/doctor_agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T05:28:02.539719Z","id":"955f73cc0b4c8877cae41663d28e10a50fb748fd87365c88a170397d74968b98","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-cli/src/commands/doctor_agent.rs:550-552, record 913befb9.\n\nNot taken (2026-10-01, docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-01-grok-build.md:113 (Q3)): Grok Build 1.0.45 and later, warned by doctor only (MIN_GROK). A different minimum changes this warning and the contract's measurement line; enforcing it would add a version check to the shim or the hooks.","kind":"alternative","ref":"git:03275e894a555fae4b08ac4bddfee28327965aed","span":{"start":{"line":550},"end":{"line":552},"content_hash":"08f4786b8e87c9b1ee9c6633438a61b1ef298ae07c9c75f84ab8067ba94831bc"},"summary":"Enforce a minimum Grok Build version instead of warning in doctor only","tags":["revisit:a Grok Build release older than MIN_GROK breaks Clax in the field","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-commands/src/commands/hook.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T05:28:02.539783Z","id":"92b616db5c1af64a9067862b353bd4df5bc7ba40d4b865f7f18446ebcc0ac5df","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-cli/src/commands/hook.rs:607-607, record 3795ed68.\n\nMutations, each run against the connect, remote and clips tests: the hook's `clax_core::clips::check(ct.as_deref(), &bytes)?` replaced by a no-op survived; the shim's check in clip_bytes replaced by a no-op survived. clips::tests::a_clip_is_checked_before_it_is_kept tests check() alone, and only Pi's remote.test.ts serves a non-PNG clip.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:03275e894a555fae4b08ac4bddfee28327965aed","span":{"start":{"line":607},"end":{"line":607},"content_hash":"8cc42c560ef2a439d5a9af5ecb2cce73595dfed3e5b1e6ddd18358b69affce8b"},"suggested_fix":"Serve one clip as text/html (or as image/png without the PNG signature) in connect::a_remote_hook_prints_its_comments_when_clips_do_not_come and remote::a_remote_clip_that_does_not_come_never_holds_the_feedback, and assert `Clip: unavailable (not a PNG)`.","summary":"No Rust test reaches the clip check in either client: removing clips::check from the hook's fetch, or from the shim's clip_bytes (crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs:1203), passes every test","tags":["review","tests","remote","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-commands/src/commands/doctor_agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:01:30.730616Z","id":"d43c598db73c7cc0cc94d333a102c52b5609a9e1d2c1132f4b16507382ae3d75","body":{"detail":"The bundled skill text doctor compares (lines 74-86, include_str! of plugins/*/skills/clax/SKILL.md) is the one embedded input left in clax-commands: every other file the binary carries reaches the commands through clax_core::embedded::Bundle (crates/clax-commands/src/lib.rs). crates/clax-commands/BUILD.bazel lists //plugins:embedded and //plugins/pi:embedded as compile_data for it.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":74},"end":{"line":86},"content_hash":"edd4ed6e6e3134739314ff324194286b15ea0315b99b6b2e273510435281a109"},"suggested_fix":"Read the skill through crate::embedded().plugins().get(\"<plugin>/skills/clax/SKILL.md\") and drop the include_str!s and the compile_data.","summary":"doctor --agent compiles the plugins' SKILL.md files into clax-commands, so a skill edit rebuilds the commands","tags":["layout","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-commands/src/commands/doctor.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:42:33.843626Z","id":"1670626d8e735ba94dd546ddfe78a7ef9406544dc7eeb7d9222a5bd6abe636c3","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-cli/src/commands/doctor.rs:730-730, record 30b40937.\n\nFailure: after an upgrade, before the daemon is replaced, `clax doctor` runs Store::open, which plans and records the backfill (seconds on a large home, with no progress shown). Changes the still-running older daemon makes after that plan are never recorded: they are not in the staging snapshot, and the older build records nothing live.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":731},"end":{"line":731},"content_hash":"e8cfaa20dc14468f4bef01aba5ada983db7554d9886c28787dbaec157f0587e0"},"suggested_fix":"Have doctor and init open the store without the backfill (or read-only) when the schema is behind and a daemon is running, and leave the backfill to the daemon's start, which reports progress.","summary":"clax doctor (and clax init's credential revoke) open the store directly, so the first run of a new build migrates to 23 and runs the whole backfill outside the daemon, silently, possibly under an older running daemon","supersedes":"1063c57c400aed342a7fa85ad5b1baa80e3d4897960a6d09f628849c61e1d2eb","tags":["review","migration","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-commands/src/commands/publish.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:33.451468Z","id":"af522cfb49b7ec5640a9966fbd71825b2205add977c426828227e03d5001b9ec","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-commands/src/commands/tools.rs:1-2 says the CLI runs the MCP tools 'so the CLI and the tools share one implementation and one JSON shape', and read, db and asset do. publish.rs copies TEXT_EXT (publish.rs:54 vs crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs:52), file_entry (publish.rs:58 vs tools.rs:775), the title rule and the if_version default (publish.rs:168-186 vs tools.rs:1340-1388). They have drifted: the tool refuses a supporting file named index.html (tools.rs:1329-1333) while `clax publish --file x.html=index.html` silently replaces the page given as the positional argument (publish.rs:125-128), and the CLI's --dir mirroring has no tool counterpart. Any fix to one (for example the if_version default) has to be made twice.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":54},"end":{"line":190},"content_hash":"e53bffa825b897224eb7ad8e24be82713681be66f1e9cd41fa76b9976955f4c3"},"suggested_fix":"Build PublishArgs from the CLI's arguments (index as file_path, --file and --dir entries as files, mirroring computed as null entries) and run ClaxTools::publish through commands::tools::call, keeping only the --dir walk and the printing in publish.rs.","summary":"clax publish re-implements the publish tool instead of calling it, so the CLI and MCP publish rules already differ","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-commands/src/commands/publish.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:01.495738Z","id":"3e5499a9c17adcb0ea79aa4dba07e1f3e5e72ee9bf4e2483a052c2ce9d12db07","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-commands/src/commands/tools.rs:1-2 states the CLI runs the MCP tools to share one implementation. crates/clax-commands/src/commands/publish.rs:54-56 (TEXT_EXT) and 58-75 (file_entry) copy crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs:52-54 and 775ff; publish.rs:144-186 copies the title rule and if_version default of tools.rs:1340-1388. Divergence: tools.rs:1329-1333 refuses a `files` key of index.html, while publish.rs:123-127 does files.insert(dest, ...) for each --file spec, so `--file x.html=index.html` replaces the positional page without error. The if_version fallback also differs (tools.rs:1385 unwrap_or(0) vs publish.rs:172-174 .context error).","kind":"comment","references":"af522cfb49b7ec5640a9966fbd71825b2205add977c426828227e03d5001b9ec","summary":"confirmed: clax publish duplicates the publish tool's logic and already diverges on index.html in --file","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-commands/src/commands/publish.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:53:12.881843Z","id":"dafe2b03b11e605d061dc4d862dbd07fbb9e6d6b23a96d7b6940a2a41731c943","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c42b7c9","summary":"Fixed: clax publish runs ClaxTools::publish via commands::tools::call_on; cli.rs::publish_follows_the_publish_tools_rules passes and the existing CLI publish tests pass.","supersedes":"af522cfb49b7ec5640a9966fbd71825b2205add977c426828227e03d5001b9ec","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-commands/src/commands/bin.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T16:40:20.756069Z","id":"06c374df3b2783dd084018eaffbd153db1c81d496dc04bfc852cca238e4f5a6f","body":{"detail":"Both name this binary by std::env::current_exe (also crates/clax-commands/src/commands/init.rs:848). On Linux that is /proc/self/exe, with every symbolic link resolved; on macOS it is the path the binary was run by. A Linux install reached through a link to a versioned directory (a package manager's cellar, for example) records the versioned path, which an upgrade removes; the same install on macOS records the link. Seen in CI run 39440289806, where Bazel's runfiles link was recorded as the execroot file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":56},"end":{"line":56},"content_hash":"b3525db7fb321a16f1a366a7d5d06da5161bebad747f1f21de322b61170da65c"},"summary":"bin set --this and init record a symlink-resolved path on Linux and the path run on macOS","tags":["linux","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-commands/src/commands/doctor.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:02:19.511105Z","id":"b2c2493a6342a78f5c8795eccec2d56d5f54cba691a1ad117a8ec8a899032f7b","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-cli/src/commands/doctor.rs:730-730, record 30b40937.\n\nFailure: after an upgrade, before the daemon is replaced, `clax doctor` runs Store::open, which plans and records the backfill (seconds on a large home, with no progress shown). Changes the still-running older daemon makes after that plan are never recorded: they are not in the staging snapshot, and the older build records nothing live.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":783},"end":{"line":783},"content_hash":"e8cfaa20dc14468f4bef01aba5ada983db7554d9886c28787dbaec157f0587e0"},"suggested_fix":"Have doctor and init open the store without the backfill (or read-only) when the schema is behind and a daemon is running, and leave the backfill to the daemon's start, which reports progress.","summary":"clax doctor (and clax init's credential revoke) open the store directly, so the first run of a new build migrates to 23 and runs the whole backfill outside the daemon, silently, possibly under an older running daemon","supersedes":"1670626d8e735ba94dd546ddfe78a7ef9406544dc7eeb7d9222a5bd6abe636c3","tags":["review","migration","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-commands/src/commands/comments.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T18:18:56.142601Z","id":"b7065c6d58f64872847a23c0b2dba0a6a3139ed1256185d949381b97aa120896","body":{"detail":"Failure: a headless agent that runs one harness turn per wake and posts with 'clax comments reply' (token, no X-Clax-Session) writes author_kind viewer comments under the owner viewer's public ID and name; participants.people lists it as the owner (named whatever the agent set with 'clax comments name'), and participants.agents (crates/clax-store/src/attention.rs agents_sql) cannot see it. An agent reply (author_kind agent with X-Clax-Session, crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs comment) is listed since the commit that adds comment sessions to agents_sql, but only on sent threads, and a per-turn session has ended by the next look, so it shows under Earlier. Proposal: a --session option on 'clax comments reply' that sends author_kind agent with that session; and serialise each listed agent's activity time so the shell keeps an ended agent active within a few minutes in Agents rather than Earlier (live stays as is: it means a send reaches it).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":10},"end":{"line":13},"content_hash":"6f9a6294827f3cba8f3c8a06725ee2f6f439674df17170b22e07c7a7ae74c783"},"summary":"An agent that replies through clax comments reply is the owner person, never an agent, so the People panel lists no agent for its work","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:2f9bedcd-d2fb-4118-b567-9d2ab734c766"]}}
